The library board of trustees shall have duties and responsibilities which include, but are not limited to, the following:
(1) To employ a library director who meets state certification requirements and to whom the board of trustees may delegate the authority for hiring other staff as needed to carry out the responsibilities of providing service to the county. All staff shall serve at the pleasure of the Gwinnett County Public Library Board of Trustees. The library director shall be responsible for administering the total library program in accordance with policies adopted by the library board of trustees;
(2) To approve budgets prepared by the library system director and assume responsibility for the presentation of the library's fiscal needs to the supporting agencies;
(3) To attend board meetings;
(4) To establish policies governing library programs, including rules and regulations governing the use of the library;
(5) To adopt bylaws under which the board of trustees will operate;
(6) To set policy for the administration of gifts of money and property;
(7) To present financial and progress reports to the board of commissioners and to the public;
(8) To notify the board of commissioners of a vacancy on the board so that a person may be appointed to complete unexpired or full terms;
(9) To notify the library system director, in advance, of all meetings of the board of trustees and its committees;
(10) To enter into contracts for the benefit of the library;
(11) To expend appropriated funds in accordance with the budget of the library;
(12) To accept donations of money, land and other property for the use and benefit of the library; the title to any land to be taken in the name of the county; and
(13) To hold property, including land, buildings, books and other equipment, for the use and benefit of the library; the title to any land to be taken in the name of the county.
(Code 1994, § 66-35; Ord. of 9-17-2002, § 1)

